Subject: [PATCH 25/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV requests: workload metadata

CausalKVRequest gains two optional fields, generation_index (int) and
workload (plain-JSON dict), both None by default. The causal denoising
stage fills them from req.extra["workload"] (CAUSAL_KV_WORKLOAD_KEY;
validated by causal_kv_workload_metadata: a JSON object, copied, with an
optional non-negative int generation_index) when it hands a request to an
attached backend. They are request metadata for unhashed sidecars and
request records (the workload runner's generation index and its own
record), never part of the conditioning identity or any hash and not a
session (routing) field; CausalKVRequest.request_id stays the SGLang
request id. Without the key the request is exactly as before; without a
backend it is never read. New unit test
test/unit/test_wl_request_metadata.py.
